441
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:00,840
technique.

442
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:05,180
It's a very bare bones way of
producing reasoning techniques

443
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:07,180
in a model.

444
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:10,860
And the assumption that is being
made in this particular case

445
00:20:10,860 --> 00:20:13,920
is that how do you know
something is a good rationale?

446
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:16,400
They're assuming that if
the model output is correct,

447
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:19,500
which in math they found
that was generally true,

448
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:21,460
the correctness of
the final output

449
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:23,615
is a proxy for the
reasoning quality.

450
00:20:23,615 --> 00:20:25,240
So they're filtering
incorrect answers.

451
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:29,060
Basically, they're assuming
that will be filtering out

452
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:30,860
lower quality reasoning
chains, but there

453
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:33,900
might be scenarios
where they're not

454
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:37,180
learning from incorrect
reasoning chains as a result.

455
00:20:37,180 --> 00:20:39,640
But they get higher
quality training data.

456
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:43,460
And then the second bit is that
they assume that the language

457
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:46,380
model can generate valid
reasoning paths when it's

458
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:47,920
given the answer as a hint.

459
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:50,580
So it assumes that if I
show the model the answer

460
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:53,780
and then ask it to show its
work, it will be able to do so.

461
00:20:53,780 --> 00:20:57,420
And then finally, there is
some amount of assumption

462
00:20:57,420 --> 00:20:59,540
that the initial language
model is strong enough

463
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:02,160
to bootstrap from
few short examples.

464
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:04,300
So if the class of
problems is way outside

465
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:06,960
the capability of the
initial language model,

466
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:09,837
then it will not make
much progress on this.

467
00:21:09,837 --> 00:21:11,420
And this is where
the iterative aspect

468
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:13,300
starts to become important.

